From 95d49054c2829f282a0b543355836a9abf23ee79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:09:09 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] SHLD r/m16, r16, 16: CF by the double-wide rule,
 upstream 6646a5cc behind MACRUNNER_FEX_SHLD16_CF

Upstream FEX 6646a5cc ("Fixes SHLD by 16 behaviour", 25 Aug 2026) behind a gate for this series: for the
double-wide shift a count equal to the operand width is defined (CF = the last bit shifted out of the
destination); only a larger count is undefined. CalculateFlags_ShiftLeftImmediate gets the DoubleWide
argument as upstream; with MACRUNNER_FEX_SHLD16_CF=1 (default off) SHLDImmediateOp uses it. The upstream
unit test SHLD_CF.asm is not carried over, since it fails with the gate off.

MacRunnerShld16CfApplied counts SHLD translations whose CF the gate changed (count == width); a
macrunner-fex-shld16-cf line is printed at 1, 2, 4, ... HB<->FEX oracle: 3 of 3 SHLD-16 cases become
x86-correct, no other result changes.

